menu "SeaTalk bridge"

    config ST_BRIDGE_BENCH
        bool "Bench console on USB serial (key commands, statistics)"
        default y
        help
            Compile the bench console: single-key commands on the USB serial
            port (self-test, RX monitor, datagram table, statistics). Costs one
            4 KB task. Without it the board runs only the bridge itself.

    config ST_BRIDGE_TELNET
        bool "Telnet console (port 23, unauthenticated: bench use only)"
        default n
        depends on ST_BRIDGE_BENCH
        help
            Compile the telnet mirror of the bench console. It is compiled in
            only; at run time it is started and stopped by the espOS config
            setting bench.telnet (default off) and uses no RAM while off.
            The console has no authentication: anyone on the LAN can send keys.

    config ST_BRIDGE_SIM
        bool "Simulated boat (demo values to the bus, keys v/V)"
        default n
        depends on ST_BRIDGE_BENCH
        help
            Compile the simulated boat, which feeds demo values to the bus
            (keys v and V in the bench console).

endmenu
